      "id": 1,
      "text": "Stone Mountain Park, the centerpiece of Mountain Park, opened in 1963 as Historic Square before becoming the iconic granite landmark it is today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stone_Mountain",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The park hosted Olympic events in 1996, providing venues for tennis, archery, and track cycling during the Summer Games.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stone_Mountain",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 2020, activists formed the Stone Mountain Action Coalition to push for a more inclusive park that reflects the region’s diverse history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stone_Mountain",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A proposed Freedom Bell honoring Martin Luther King Jr. was discussed in 2015, reflecting ongoing debates over the park’s Confederate imagery.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stone_Mountain",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The park’s granite quarry began in the 1830s, growing into a major industry after a railroad spur reached the site in 1847.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
